      "writtenOn": "2019-04-01T20:14:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "do we have some check at higher levels that makes sure that we have space in nvmem? probably not, since that\u0027d require to know the exact state of the underlying pages (or at the very least the total size of all vars and all nvmem objects to make sure they still should fit)?\n\nif we don\u0027t have a soft-check, a user can cause keep creating \u0026 writing nvram spaces until TPM goes out of boundaries trying to allocate a new page for an already full nvmem. I\u0027d suggest returning an error through the call stack in case there\u0027s not enough space instead of turning that into a catastrophic error.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 905,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 905,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "5417d05a27ebeaf5139257d85214dda7bf4988df",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02d84f96_3b14e066",
        "filename": "common/new_nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 905,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-01T22:41:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The TPM library checks room in the NVMEM cache before trying to add an object, by design flash storage is supposed to guarantee to accommodate the cache contents.\n\nWe could experience this failure also during compaction, and in that case there is no point in returning an error, something must be really messed up, this is why I think failing here unconditionally is a better signal.",
      "parentUuid": "01d12f36_0e6a78e0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 905,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 905,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "5417d05a27ebeaf5139257d85214dda7bf4988df",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4eeea253_5b4fe29c",
        "filename": "common/new_nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 905,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-02T19:03:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This, I suspect, is the one and only important remaining issue with this CL.\nIf we can guarantee that if the objects fit into a cache they are guaranteed to fit into flash pages, then yes, we can go with die-if-fail-to-alloc page approach, since it is all checked at a higher level. and this might be the main reason to enforce that max 1000 bytes in k,v tuples limitation (otherwise it\u0027s just a waste of code size to do those checks imo): basically, we need to guarantee that cache contents + 1000 bytes always fit in flash (assuming all pages are healthy - if pages start becoming unwritable/unerasable then yes, we can die).\nIf we can\u0027t guarantee that, then we need a soft-error, I\u0027m afraid. Again, can change in a separate CL to avoid stalling this one, but needs to go in before this feature is considered ready for prepvt.",
      "parentUuid": "02d84f96_3b14e066",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 905,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 905,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "5417d05a27ebeaf5139257d85214dda7bf4988df",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
